From 73ba71bdbe99ff6cde5133b658773727187fa07e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Aw <zachary_aw@outlook.sg>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 14:22:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] vulkan: add GGML_OP_DSV4_HC_SPLIT_SINKHORN kernel

Hyperconnection split + Sinkhorn normalization for DeepSeek-V4. Each row of
mixes ([(2 + n_hc)*n_hc, n_rows]) becomes n_hc pre gates (sigmoid + eps),
n_hc post gates (2*sigmoid), and an n_hc x n_hc comb matrix that is
row-softmaxed (+eps) and then Sinkhorn-normalized: one column pass followed
by sinkhorn_iters - 1 further (row, column) pairs, each dividing by
(sum + eps).

One workgroup (64 threads) per row, with the comb matrix in a 16x16 shared
array (n_hc <= 16 is asserted by the CPU op and gated in supports_op).
Every reduction - the softmax max/sum and both Sinkhorn passes - runs
serially inside a single thread over the same ascending index order as
ggml_compute_forward_dsv4_hc_split_sinkhorn (ggml-cpu/ops.cpp) and
kernel_dsv4_hc_split_sinkhorn (ggml-metal.metal), with c indexed
[src_hc + dst_hc*n_hc] exactly like the CPU reference, so the only numeric
difference vs the CPU is exp() vs expf(). The barriers between phases sit
in workgroup-uniform control flow (the row early-out is uniform, and
sinkhorn_iters is a push constant).

Wired through the generic vk_op_f32 path (3 srcs -> 4 bindings), sharing the
rows-split elements/dispatch group with DSV4_FP8_KV_QUANTIZE, with
supports_op mirroring the Metal gate plus the n_hc <= 16 and ne2/ne3 == 1
bounds the shader relies on. test-backend-ops coverage: canonical prefill
and 1-token decode, sinkhorn_iters 1/2/3/8, n_hc 1/2/4/8/16, non-contiguous
mixes rows, 1024 rows (y-split dispatch), eps = 0, saturating inputs with
eps-dominated columns, and tiny values with tiny eps. 14/14 pass on RADV
GFX1151.

sinkhorn_iters = 0 is not tested: ggml_dsv4_hc_split_sinkhorn asserts
sinkhorn_iters > 0, so no such node can reach a backend.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
